source      RDKit's UFF atom typing, RDKit::UFF::Tools::getAtomLabel, called per atom through
            bb-rdkit's cxx bridge (bb-rdkit::uff_atom_labels -> bb::uff_atom_labels in bridge.cc)
            on the post-AddHs molecule. getAtomLabel is exported by RDKit; the bridge calls it and
            copies the string, computing nothing itself.
purpose     gate for the pure-Rust UFF atom-typing port (bb_perceive::uff::atom_label). That port
            reproduces the full getAtomLabel + addAtomChargeFlags source (every element branch); this
            fixture is the gate over real molecules, NOT the source of truth for which rules to
            implement. The UFF parameter table is vendored verbatim in rdkit-patch/uff_params.txt
            (dumped from ForceFields::UFF::defaultParamData via bb-rdkit::uff_param_table).
format      JSONL, one object per corpus line:
            {"name": <id>, "labels": [<UFF type string per atom, post-AddHs order>]}
            A SMILES RDKit cannot parse is {"name": <id>, "error": "unparseable"} rather than
            dropped, so the count matches the corpus.
corpus      first 600 of validation/seeds_5000.smi (same molecule set as raw_bounds_seeds600)
indices     post-AddHs atom order (RDKit SmilesToMol + addHs)
generated   2026-08-14
